@page "/dbcontext-factory-comparison"
@rendermode @(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))

<PageTitle>DbContext factory comparison</PageTitle>

<h1>DbContext factory comparison</h1>

<p class="lead">
    This page keeps the same component fan-out and the same scoped service lifetime, but each lookup creates a fresh
    EF Core <code>AppDbContext</code> through <code>IDbContextFactory&lt;AppDbContext&gt;</code>.
</p>

<div class="alert alert-success" role="alert">
    Expected result: all cards should load successfully, and the <code>DbContext ID</code> values should differ between
    cards even though the service ID stays the same within the circuit.
</div>

<div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-2 row-cols-xl-3 g-4">
    <div class="col">
        <FactoryUserLookupCard Title="Component A" UserId="1" />
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <FactoryUserLookupCard Title="Component B" UserId="2" />
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <FactoryUserLookupCard Title="Component C" UserId="3" />
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <FactoryUserLookupCard Title="Component D" UserId="4" />
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <FactoryUserLookupCard Title="Component E" UserId="5" />
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <FactoryUserLookupCard Title="Component F" UserId="6" />
    </div>
</div>
